<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN">  <HTML><HEAD><TITLE></TITLE>  <META http-equiv=Content-Type content="text/html; charset=unicode">  <META content="MSHTML 6.00.2800.1400" name=GENERATOR></HEAD>  <BODY><p>Hi, </p>
<p>I am an Atlanta based web designer/developer named Kweku. I am writing to share some very exciting news with you about <a href="http://www.myafronet.com/">www.MyAfronet.com</a> . I am not trying to sell you anything. Neither am I going to ask you to send me money for my dead grand-mother's funeral. So please read on. I also have no intentions of offending you given that this email is unsolicited. </p>
<p>I have just launched a web-based community platform, <a href="http://www.myafronet.com/">www.MyAfronet.com</a>, for Africans around the world that promises to be very successful. Best of all, it is completely FREE and very feature loaded. <strong>My mission</strong> is simple: to create the largest global business and social networking community for Africans on the web that is completely user contributed and FREE. I would like to present you with an early opportunity to become an integral part of what is destined to make the news in a short time to come. </p>
<p>At the moment, the site is completely empty but I assure you this should not deter you from joining. It is empty for a good reason: it is empty because it is yours to populate. The process is very simple and will only take a few minutes of your time. </p>
<p>
<ul>
<li>1. Sign Up.</li> 
<li>2. Login and put up your business/social profile.</li>  
<li>3. Begin networking with other members and watch your network grow.</li> 
</ul>
</p>
<p>Why am I doing this for free? I don't know about you but time and time again I have had the need to network with Africans on the web and my efforts have left me very frustrated and disillusioned for one very obvious reason: we have no major member contributed site that serves our networking needs.  Once again, I invite you to join me in making history.  You stand to benefit tremendously from your participation through networking. </p>
<p>Sincerely, </p>
<p>Kweku <br>
<a href="http://www.myafronet.com/">www.MyAfronet.com </a></p>
